  "sections": [
    {
      "title": "async def vs def Endpoints",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 0,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "async def vs def Endpoints",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Where each runs",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==async def== runs directly on the **event loop**",
                "==def== is sent to a **threadpool** (anyio, 40 threads default)",
                "Rule: async def only if every await is {green:async-native}",
                "Blocking libs (`requests`, `psycopg2`, `time.sleep`) → plain {red:def}"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "async def",
                "def"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Concurrency",
                  "Cheap",
                  "Limited by thread count"
                ],
                [
                  "Blocking call",
                  "{red:Stalls ALL requests}",
                  "Isolated per request"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Example",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`/a` and `/b` stay responsive; `/c` ==freezes the server=="
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "python",
              "lines": [
                "@app.get('/a')",
                "async def a(): await asyncio.sleep(1)",
                "@app.get('/b')",
                "def b(): time.sleep(1)",
                "@app.get('/c')",
                "async def c(): time.sleep(1)  # bad"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Mistake",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Blocking code inside async def: `requests.get`, sync DB driver, CPU loops"
              ],
              "style": "cross"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Fix",
              "text": "Use plain `def`, or `await run_in_threadpool(fn)` / `await asyncio.to_thread(fn)`."
            },
            {
              "type": "sidebox",
              "title": "Interview Point",
              "items": [
                "**Why doesn't def block the loop?** It runs in a threadpool.",
                "**async def calls requests.get?** Every request stalls; use def or to_thread."
              ],
              "ink": "orange"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "SQLAlchemy 2.0 Async Engine and Session",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 1,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "SQLAlchemy 2.0 Async Engine and Session",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Engine and Factory",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`create_async_engine('postgresql+asyncpg://...')` needs an ==async driver==",
                "Drivers: `asyncpg`, `aiosqlite`; a **sync** driver URL fails",
                "`async_sessionmaker(engine, expire_on_commit=False)` is the session factory",
                "`expire_on_commit=False`: attributes are ==not expired== after commit",
                "Why: an expired attribute reloads lazily, which is illegal IO in async"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Queries and Writes",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "2.0 style: `await session.execute(select(...))`, then a result method",
                "Write: `add`, `await commit()`, then `await refresh(obj)` for server-generated fields"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "python",
              "lines": [
                "async def demo(session):",
                "    r = await session.execute(select(User).where(User.id == 1))",
                "    user = r.scalar_one_or_none()",
                "    obj = User(name=\"Ada\")",
                "    session.add(obj)",
                "    await session.commit()",
                "    await session.refresh(obj)"
              ],
              "note": "fragment: needs a live AsyncSession"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. MissingGreenlet",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Fix",
                "Use"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Main",
                  "`selectinload()` / `joinedload()` in the query"
                ],
                [
                  "Fallback",
                  "`await session.run_sync(fn)` or `awaitable_attrs`"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Mistake",
              "text": "Lazy-loading a relationship in async raises ==MissingGreenlet=="
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "4. Interview Point",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "**Why expire_on_commit=False?** Expired attributes reload lazily, illegal IO in async.",
                "**Why MissingGreenlet?** Attribute access hit the DB outside an await; eager-load instead."
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "ink": "purple"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Session per Request via Dependencies",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 2,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Session per Request via Dependencies",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. The Pattern",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==One AsyncSession per request==, created in a dependency",
                "`get_db` is an **async generator**; code after `yield` is cleanup",
                "Inject: `db: Annotated[AsyncSession, Depends(get_db)]`",
                "Sub-dependencies in one request share the ==same session== (dependency cache)"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Request",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Open session",
                    "sub": "async with",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Endpoint runs",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Exception?",
                    "sub": "rollback",
                    "ink": "red"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Close",
                    "sub": "always",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "python",
              "lines": [
                "async def get_db():",
                "    async with SessionLocal() as session:",
                "        try:",
                "            yield session",
                "        except Exception:",
                "            await session.rollback()",
                "            raise"
              ],
              "note": "rollback only if an exception propagates"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Transactions",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Commit is ==explicit==: `await session.commit()` in endpoint or service",
                "Rollback runs only when an ==exception propagates==",
                "After commit, loaded attributes expire; touching them is lazy IO and fails ({red:MissingGreenlet})",
                "Fix: `expire_on_commit=False` or `await session.refresh(obj)`"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Mistakes",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Global session shared across requests: not concurrency safe",
                "One session shared between `asyncio.gather` tasks"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "One task, one session",
              "text": "A session is never shared across requests or concurrent tasks. Give each its own."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Background Tasks",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 3,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Background Tasks",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. What It Does",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`background_tasks.add_task(send_email, to, body)`",
                "Runs ==after the response is sent==",
                "{blue:def} task → threadpool; {green:async def} task → event loop",
                "Args after the function are passed to `add_task`"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Endpoint",
                    "sub": "add_task",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Response sent",
                    "sub": "client done",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Task runs",
                    "sub": "after",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Task Runner or Queue",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "BackgroundTasks",
                "Celery / ARQ / RQ"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Use for",
                  "Short fire-and-forget: emails, logs",
                  "Heavy or durable jobs"
                ],
                [
                  "Process dies",
                  "{red:Task lost}",
                  "{green:Job survives}"
                ],
                [
                  "Retries",
                  "{red:None}",
                  "{green:Built in}"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Example and Mistake",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Endpoint adds the task, returns ==immediately==",
                "Task opens its ==own session=="
              ],
              "style": "number"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "python",
              "lines": [
                "async def signup(u: UserIn, background_tasks: BackgroundTasks):",
                "    background_tasks.add_task(send_welcome, u.email)",
                "    return {\"status\": \"queued\"}",
                "async def send_welcome(to: str):",
                "    async with SessionLocal() as s:",
                "        await s.execute(insert(EmailLog).values(to=to))",
                "        await s.commit()"
              ],
              "note": "call site plus task body"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Mistake: reusing the request's DB session in the task",
                "The dependency session is already **closed**"
              ],
              "style": "cross"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Fix",
              "text": "Open a new session inside the task with `SessionLocal()`."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Lifespan Events",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 4,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Lifespan Events",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. What lifespan is",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==lifespan== is an `@asynccontextmanager` passed as `FastAPI(lifespan=lifespan)`",
                "Code {green:before `yield`} runs at ==startup==",
                "Code {red:after `yield`} runs at ==shutdown=="
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Startup and shutdown work",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "python",
              "lines": [
                "@asynccontextmanager",
                "async def lifespan(app: FastAPI):",
                "    engine = create_async_engine(DB_URL)",
                "    app.state.engine = engine",
                "    app.state.SessionLocal = async_sessionmaker(",
                "        engine, expire_on_commit=False)",
                "    yield",
                "    await engine.dispose()"
              ],
              "note": "engine built once, disposed once"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Phase",
                "Typical work"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Startup",
                  "async engine + sessionmaker, load ML models, Redis or HTTP client pools"
                ],
                [
                  "Store on",
                  "`app.state`"
                ],
                [
                  "Shutdown",
                  "`await engine.dispose()`, close clients, flush resources"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 0
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Old way and mistakes",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "lifespan replaces deprecated `@app.on_event('startup')` and `'shutdown'`",
                "Do not mix both styles in one app"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Engine created per request instead of once in lifespan",
                "Forgot `engine.dispose()`: connections leak on shutdown"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Remember",
              "text": "One engine per app: ==create before yield==, ==dispose after yield==."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "FastAPI Async Cheat Sheet",
      "role": "outline",
